<!DOCTYPE html>
{#
    A page whose form came back with errors sets "form_invalid" to true (a top-level set in the page
    template): the title then starts with "Error:" (WCAG 3.3.1), and the form-errors controller on the
    body moves the focus to the first invalid field.
    The document title runs from the specific to the general, "Page · Section · Foresi" (page_title);
    a frame overrides the block "document_title" to give the section, or to leave the product out.
#}
<html lang="{{ app.request.locale }}">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8">
        {#
            viewport-fit=cover lets the page run under the notch and the home indicator; the shell, the
            dialogs and the bars pad themselves with env(safe-area-inset-*) (WebKit, "Designing Websites
            for iPhone X"). Pinch zoom stays on: no maximum-scale, no user-scalable=no.
        #}
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
        {# Turbo cross-fades the content panel between pages; the shell sets which part moves. #}
        <meta name="view-transition" content="same-origin">
        {#
            The icon is the Foresi mark of the rail, the green square with the F, drawn as a path so it
            needs no font. It is inline: an SVG scales to every size the browser asks for, and img-src
            of the Content-Security-Policy allows data: URLs. A frame without the product overrides the
            block "icon".
        #}
        {% block icon %}{% set icon %}<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 32 32"><rect width="32" height="32" rx="4" fill="#2f4a3a"/><path fill="#fff" d="M10.5 7.5h11v3.4h-7.2v3.6h6.3v3.3h-6.3v6.7h-3.8z"/></svg>{% endset %}
        <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="data:image/svg+xml,{{ icon|url_encode }}">{% endblock %}
        {# The block "title" is the page's heading; it is defined here and read where it is needed. #}
        {% set heading %}{% block title %}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
        <title>{% if form_invalid|default(false) %}{{ 'form.title_error'|trans }} {% endif %}{% block document_title %}{{ page_title(heading|striptags|html_decode|trim) }}{% endblock %}</title>
        {% block head %}{% endblock %}
        {% block stylesheets %}{% endblock %}
        {% block javascripts %}
            {#
                The nonce of this response's Content-Security-Policy, only on a page that runs scripts.
                Turbo gives it to the scripts and the progress bar style it adds; it reads the nonce
                property, so the value is not in "content", and the tag is the same on every page, so a
                visit keeps the first page's nonce, the one the document's policy holds (Turbo,
                getCspNonce and HeadSnapshot).
            #}
            <meta name="csp-nonce" nonce="{{ csp_nonce() }}">
            {% block importmap %}{{ importmap('app', {nonce: csp_nonce()}) }}{% endblock %}
        {% endblock %}
    </head>
    <body data-controller="form-errors"{% block body_attributes %}{% endblock %}>
        {% block body %}{% endblock %}
    </body>
</html>
